Excellent advice.

I suggest using a capital letter that does not carry any other meaning
in NetHack, because they are harder to hit accidentally when you are
entering lots of lower-case NetHack commands. Personally, I use N,M,O
for things that should not go in the bag of holding (cancellation, bag
of tricks, cross-aligned artifacts, artifacts with when-carried
effects, luckstone etc). Similarily, I always use "a" for the bag of
holding because accessing stuff with "aa" is much less prone to typos
than combinations involving different keys.

The !"$%/()=3D?[] keys can and should be habitually used at the loot
menu. It's hard to put your wand of cancellation into the bag of
holding if "." selects only, say, scrolls. (This is a patch, NAO has
it.)

Some people advise setting cancellation to early letters in the
alphabet. The idea is that more valueable stuff would enter the bag
later, when it has already been exploded and cannot destroy the
valuables along with it.

Finally, there is no substitute for typing carefully.

More on this subject: http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Adjust#Strategy


